---
const stages = [
  ['01','Ingest','Authenticated generic and Grafana webhooks become normalized, idempotent events.','events'],
  ['02','Correlate','Versioned rules create or extend compatible incident lifecycles.','incidents + outbox'],
  ['03','Investigate','A bounded agent queries configured Prometheus and Loki adapters.','runs + evidence'],
  ['04','Report','Daily and high-severity requests produce durable multi-incident reports.','reports + attempts'],
  ['05','Review','Human feedback measures correctness, usefulness, and false confidence.','reviews + feedback'],
];
const principles = [
  ['Never fabricate evidence','Unavailable sources return unavailable. They never return sample observations.'],
  ['Unknown is a valid result','Contradictory or insufficient evidence ends in an explicit unknown, not a guessed RCA.'],
  ['Commit before side effects','PostgreSQL transactions and outboxes preserve state before remote work begins.'],
];
---
<section id="workflow" class="workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-heading reveal-item">
      <p class="eyebrow">The canonical workflow</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-title">Structure first.<br/>Reason inside boundaries.</h2>
      <p>Every stage owns its writes. Retries may repeat transport, but idempotency prevents duplicate durable effects.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="workflow-track">
      {stages.map(([number,title,body,output], index) => <li class="workflow-card reveal-item" style={`--reveal-delay:${index * 55}ms`}>
        <div class="workflow-number">{number}</div><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></div><code>{output}</code>
      </li>)}
    </ol>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      {principles.map(([title,body], index) => <article class="principle-card reveal-item" style={`--reveal-delay:${index * 70}ms`}><span>0{index+1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
